# Garmr public-export KEEPLIST — paths the PUBLIC repository OWNS.
#
# The public repo is not a pure mirror. A curated presentation, legal, CI and
# security-documentation layer was authored directly in the public tree and has
# no counterpart here: the public README is a ~95-line public-facing summary
# (this repo's is ~267 lines and carries internal architecture detail), the
# public workflows pin every Action to a commit SHA, and the public
# docs/security + docs/status pages are written for external reviewers.
#
# Without this list, `public-export.sh` (which finalizes with `rsync --delete`)
# would DELETE every public-only file and overwrite the curated ones with this
# repo's versions — silently undoing the v0.1.0-alpha.1 release hardening.
#
# Semantics: for each path below, the export carries the version ALREADY PRESENT
# in the destination tree into the staging area before verification, so the
# verified tree is exactly what the public repo will end up with. Nothing here
# is ever generated from this repo.
#
# Rules:
#   * one path per line: a file, a directory (recursive), or a `!` exception
#   * `!path` un-keeps a path that an earlier directory rule captured — use it
#     when this repo IS the source of truth for something inside a kept dir
#   * lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored
#
# Keep this list SMALL and justified. Anything here is a place where the two
# repositories are allowed to drift, and drift is what made the first resync
# dangerous. When a file's real source of truth moves back into this repo,
# delete its line here.

# --- Legal and project identity (authored for the public release) -----------
LICENSE
LICENSES
NOTICE
COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md
TRADEMARKS.md
CLA.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
REUSE.toml
CHANGELOG.md

# --- Public-facing entry points ---------------------------------------------
# The public README is a deliberately trimmed summary, and SECURITY.md is the
# published disclosure policy. Both are maintained in the public repo.
README.md
SECURITY.md

# --- GitHub configuration and CI --------------------------------------------
# Every external Action in the public workflows is pinned to a full commit SHA
# and gated by scripts/check-actions-pinned.sh. This repo's workflows are not.
# EXCEPTION: workflows/webui.yml is authored HERE and flows outward.
.github
!.github/workflows/webui.yml

# --- Published documentation -------------------------------------------------
# docs/security, docs/status and docs/deployment are written for an external
# reviewer and are checked by scripts/check-doc-consistency.sh. docs/webui is
# NOT kept: the console documentation is authored here and flows outward.
docs
!docs/webui

# --- Supply-chain configuration and the public gates -------------------------
# deny.toml carries the audited advisory exceptions with their reachability
# analysis; the two check-* scripts are the public repo's own CI gates.
deny.toml
.gitleaks.toml
scripts/check-doc-consistency.sh
scripts/check-actions-pinned.sh

# --- The export tooling itself ------------------------------------------------
# Present in both repos; the public copies are what a reader verifies against.
scripts/public-export.sh
scripts/public-verify.sh
public-export.allowlist
public-export.denylist
public-export.keeplist

# --- Tests that cover public-only documentation claims -----------------------
crates/garmr-ingest/tests/native_auth_e2e.rs
